| log-atanh and exp-taylor | Logarithms require strictly positive arguments; exponential reduction and series terminate only within the declared finite policy and checked remainder bounds. | ``claim:numerics:primitive-bounds-agree-with-independent-oracles`` compares integral and binomial brackets; primitive_domains refuses the nonpositive logarithm. |
| sigmoid-compose and tanh-compose | Compose the admitted exponential and rational laws with their positive denominators; retain the original real question. | primitive_oracles checks independently transformed exponential brackets; primitive_limits checks tiny signed arguments and exact cancellation. |
