**Signature (Readouts)** · `sig:design:readouts` pn-readouts offers read-standing, read-title, derive-raw-snapshot and traverse-raw. Standing and title reads preserve the admitted snapshot's evidence and units. Raw Self derives from final standing and registration tenure rather than appending an authored Self act (portion{``def:epoch:raw-self-edge-reading``; derivation from final standing and registration tenure rather than an authored Self act}). Raw output is explicitly terminal and optional, with its own numerical and resource status. Observation follows (`rec:observe:decision`). Public API carriage follows (`rec:api:decision`).

{{ decision('terminal-separation', 'One-way terminal boundary', 'Classify each field by its read-sites as imported input, admission closure, required evidence, optional by-product or terminal reading. Keep optional data outside the binding dependency path, while enforcing publication of required evidence even when no formula consumes it. Vary terminal preferences and caches in tests to demonstrate that binding output remains unchanged.') }}

**Algorithm (Simple-path traversal)** · `alg:design:raw-paths` Precompute raw edge weight and determinant sign on the final snapshot. This recognition-blind signed routing service is not standing transport: its parity maxima never supply a base-allocation entry or a standing certificate (portion{``rem:epoch:shared-raw-edge-primitive``; separation of signed raw routing from standing transport}). The half-tier settlement route is a sign-preserving charter choice, not a unique construction (``lem:graph:tier-floor-sign-invariance``, ``subsec:necessity:settlement-half-routing``, ``case:necessity:settlement-half-routing-minimal-routing``, ``case:necessity:settlement-half-routing-full-routing``). Retain each bounded-depth prefix as endpoint, visited original-vertex set, parity and exact product expression; extend only to an unvisited original vertex through a routing-live nonzero-sign edge (``def:graph:raw-snapshot-path``, ``def:epoch:double-cover-bfs-state``) (portion{``prop:nodes:self-loop-neutral``; no return to a visited original vertex in the signed raw service}). Accumulate positive and negative maxima over all allowed depths, starting with the empty source path (``subsec:necessity:max-product-path-scoring``, ``case:necessity:max-product-path-scoring-sum-of-paths``) (portion{``case:necessity:positive-parity-routing-magnitude-only``; retaining separate positive and negative raw path maxima instead of discarding determinant sign}). Never merge prefixes merely because endpoint and parity agree, remove a parity-changing cycle or prune a small positive product (``alg:epoch:exact-signed-raw-traversal``).

{{ decision('raw-readings', 'Exact optional service', 'Implement bounded original-vertex-simple path enumeration with separate parity maxima and certified scalar comparisons. Keep parallel projections and all tied maximizing candidates until equality is justified. Exhaustion or an unresolved sign/product comparison returns a non-result with its reason; no approximate traversal is labelled the exact service (``rem:sorting:raw-pruning-is-implementation``).') }}

**Rule (Raw comparison)** · `rule:design:raw-comparison` Compare exact products by exact arithmetic or checked equality witnesses where possible, otherwise refine their enclosures. Retain unresolved contenders rather than choosing by discovery order. A completed service result must certify its reported maxima and parity semantics; an output enclosure or symbolic maximum may be exposed only under a profile that explicitly defines it as the exact represented result, never silently as a scalar winner. Release support follows (`rule:compatibility:pre-one`).

