**Rule (Reference wall consumption)** · `rule:design:reference-wall-consumption` A separately published reference definition is consumed only after independent replay of (`alg:design:reference-wall`), agreement of its width and cumulative tilt with the frozen compiler support and constants, and agreement of the frozen squared bleed with the defining gain's {{ numval('num:numbers:reference-squared-bleed') }}, and resolved passing floor and policy comparisons. Its delivered rational enclosure is retained separately in the bound procedure and every map record. Require K >= 2, K < 64 and enclosure.lower >= 1/(2^K - 2) before evaluating the consuming scalar questions. A rational-wall procedure keeps its existing path. The frozen ChargedPrice, ledger and compiler view remain rational and unchanged; neither enclosure endpoint replaces the charged price.

**Algorithm (Enclosed-wall fence and map)** · `alg:design:enclosed-wall-consumers` For an enclosed wall [a,b], evaluate the width fence at a. This is conservative because the deployed gain is strictly decreasing by network-v0.31.1, ``prop:epoch:wall-controller-total``: G(a) >= G(w) for every w in [a,b]. This analytic premise is cited, not established by finite samples. The conserved map instead retains [a,b] as a separate independent coordinate of the original clamp max(x,w), after the standing and any checked constant coordinates. It never substitutes a for the map wall. The complete ordered coordinate box remains in the query, attachment check and exact-repeat key. This follows [nrz rule:cas:enclosure-clamp-grammar and rule:cas:enclosure-clamp-regularity](https://github.com/naturrhythmuszentrum/naturrhythmuszentrum/blob/2628abd36f8b700c60a35e5a9134b7f7c8ed2367/crates/cas/README.md): the floor slope is zero below every wall, one above every wall and [0,1] on a touching, crossing or uncertain join. Generalized differentiation is terminal; no smooth derivative passes through the kink. Replay rebuilds the fence at the retained lower endpoint and the map with the full interval, and rejects a changed map wall scope even when an exact map branch needs no activation. Every returned solve also passes its own independent replay under maximum_replay_work; production and replay have separate charged ledgers.

