**Algorithm (Image-first box verification)** · `alg:design:two-map-verification` This is a separately declared verification route beside the default one-map projected solve. Exact source counts, affine source rates in a checked defining wall enclosure, positive retention, positive square-root base scores, full emission, ordered hop shape and exactly normalized depth masses define the map under network-v0.31.1, ``def:epoch:finite-depth-conserved-transport`` and ``def:epoch:conserved-standing-map``. The epoch adapter reconstructs the supported rational-base, full-emission case from its immutable frozen package; the reference declaration separately retains the implicit wall in its ledger formulas and never reprices a ChargedPrice. Evaluate the fence with the wall's lower endpoint and an outward upper bound on the contributing width, preserving common-wall cancellation in rate differences; strict decrease follows from ``prop:epoch:wall-controller-total``. Divide the evaluated fence upper endpoint by the exact margin to obtain c < 1. Every scalar query and attachment is retained and independently reconstructed on replay.

**Rule (Two-map residual construction)** · `rule:design:two-map-residual` Certify Y enclosing y = F(z), then evaluate the complete map on the independent coordinate box Y to obtain Z enclosing F(y). For each nonsingleton row set its residual bound to sup |Z_i - Y_i|; for a singleton-support row it is exactly zero, since F_i(F(z)) and F_i(z) are the same source rate at each fixed wall, as in ``ver:standing:conserved-equilibrium-enclosure``. Take R as the maximum of these bounds and radius = R/(1-c). The source-rate wall enclosure remains in Y and in every dependent row; it is not erased by the residual identity. The enclosure Y + [-radius,radius] contains the selected equilibrium by ``lem:dynamics:fixed-point-residual-enclosure``; y belongs to the rate hull by the pair-mediant identity. No finite-precision comparison slack is needed in this exact-endpoint proof. The separate one-map comparison uses sup |Y-z|/(1-c), after validating active candidate coordinates against inner rate-hull bounds. Singleton-support rows equal their defining source rate and have no incoming state-dependent off-diagonal term; substitute that same defining rate in the comparison and retain its wall enclosure, rather than asserting an independently equal point. Replay reconstructs both maps, both radii and the final enclosure. It refuses altered declarations, boxes, scalar questions, attachments or derived results.

**Rule (Verification endpoint schedule)** · `rule:design:verification-endpoint-schedule` The declaration fixes a positive dyadic fractional-bit grid within the scalar grid ceiling. Signed endpoint addition, subtraction, multiplication and positive-denominator division are charged rational operations followed by outward coarsening to that grid. Products retain source-adjacent factor order, normalized depth masses and full emission. These coarsenings enclose the mathematical map; derivatives must enclose that mathematical map, not differentiate its rounding algorithm. Each map has its own declared operation Work allowance, including input validation, base-root evidence, fence evidence, activation evidence, normalization, products and mediants. Residual assembly has a separate charged ledger. Operational exhaustion supplies no result. This schedule and its measured costs do not change the default solve or establish published-figure containment.

