**Algorithm (Corroborating local inclusion)** · `alg:design:local-inclusion` This is a separate local verdict beside the two-map residual under (`alg:design:two-map-verification`), following network-v0.31.1, ``ver:standing:conserved-equilibrium-enclosure``. Independently replay that residual first. Reduce singleton-support rows to their defining source rates, retaining their wall intervals as parameters; active coordinates keep their original input order. Let m be the exact midpoint of each active image enclosure Y_i. With declared inflation alpha > 1 and padding epsilon > 0, set r = alpha (radius_residual + max_i width(Y_i)/2) + epsilon and X_i = [m_i-r,m_i+r]. Require X strictly above the whole wall enclosure and inside every realized reduced rate hull for an Included verdict. These checks use outward endpoints. A failed sufficient inclusion is Unresolved, never a no-root conclusion.

**Rule (Local Jacobian and preconditioner)** · `rule:design:local-jacobian` Interval forward-mode differentiation encloses DF(X) through the same normalized hops, source-adjacent matrix products, depth mixture and pair mediants as the box map. Scalar hop derivatives are terminal generalized queries in their full independent standing and wall coordinates, under nrz's clamp grammar and regularity rules. At an uncertain join the clamp slope retains [0,1]; chain rules carry that interval into the hop derivative, and no smooth derivative crosses that join. Even a wall-touching or crossing box is evaluated with these generalized slopes and cannot receive the strictly-above-wall local verdict. Signed rational arithmetic with the declared outward grid encloses the mathematical derivatives; the rounding algorithm is never differentiated. The deterministic rational preconditioner is C = I, with denominator one. Its nonsingularity is exact. Thus K(X) = F(m) + DF(X)(X-m). Certify K(X) strictly inside X and the infinity norm of DF(X) strictly below one. Retain the Jacobian, preconditioner, box, midpoint, asserted Krawczyk image, its radius about m, all scalar queries and attachments. Reconstruct each on replay. This local root corroborates the residual's selected equilibrium through the already checked global fence; it does not replace the residual or assert published-figure agreement.

**Rule (Local Work accounting)** · `rule:design:local-work` Residual replay retains the two separate map ledgers and residual-assembly ledger. The local declaration adds its own operation allowance, bounded by the procedure's operation ceiling. Its ledger includes declaration and domain checks, base and fence evidence, F(m), all full-box hop values and derivatives, forward interval composition and the inclusion checks. Exhaustion refuses without a local verdict. The active derivative-cell census is bounded before allocation. Only the measured fixture allowance is adopted; another input receives no inferred cost guarantee.

