r possible lost correlation only widens a sound enclosure. The enclosing evidence must join these premises before it can claim the original activation. This replaces recomputation of constants across requests without granting an unchecked constant or admitting a new digest. Memoized identical requests retain identical evidence; changing the reduction ceiling, the expression or the shared constant enclosure can change presented endpoints and completion within a budget, although every returned bound remains valid. The public policy and schedule, not private reuse, determine the accepted result. (`rule:design:refinement`) still forbids truncated sequences, point substitutes and weakened comparisons.

**Decision (Activation evaluation policy)** · `dec:design:activation-evaluation-policy` One declared reduction ceiling K governs every scalar request of a procedure, including gain, activation, normalization, powers and base evaluation. For the reference bleed profile, binding checks K at least two and the frozen wall w at least 1/(2^K-2) before scalar evaluation. With p=w/(1+w), tanh(p) is at least p/(1+p)=w/(1+2w), using exp(2p) at least 1+2p; hence this lower wall bound keeps that gain logarithm argument at least 2^-K. The other gain logarithm arguments lie between one half and one, and its exponential arguments have magnitude at most two. This is a declared argument-range check, not a guarantee that finite enclosures, arbitrary rational hop powers or their complete requests finish within the allowance. The same check applies to the lower endpoint of a reference wall enclosure. An out-of-range wall refuses at binding and is never silently assigned a larger ceiling. Each changed declaration has its own Work and accuracy evidence under (`open:design:candidate-method`). The deployed gain uses one quarter of the derivative of log Q(p(x)); the constant normalization and fourth root disappear from that derivative. The clean screen remains a different quantity. Endpoint evaluation follows the monotonicity premises, and a wall crossing retains the generalized interval including zero. Every rational rung remains supported within the declared magnitude limits; root-route and log-exp-route costs are measured separately. For positive normalized values the checked dyadic quarter-power route replaces two explicit square-root nodes; the zero-capable responsive branch keeps the two-root construction. At the measured point this changes total Work from {{ numval('num:numbers:nested-root-request-work') }} to {{ numval('num:numbers:quarter-power-request-work') }} at ceiling {{ numval('num:numbers:quarter-power-reduction-ceiling') }} while reducing the output ceiling from {{ numval('num:numbers:nested-root-output-ceiling-bytes') }} to {{ numval('num:numbers:quarter-power-output-ceiling-bytes') }} bytes. The former ceiling was nrz's conservative unfolded analytic receipt reservation, not the {{ numval('num:numbers:nested-root-certificate-bytes') }}-byte certificate or live memory. The dedicated power transcript has a smaller bounded reservation and a {{ numval('num:numbers:quarter-power-certificate-bytes') }}-byte certificate. No default, domain check or independent endpoint check is relaxed. A smaller ceiling must be witnessed at its exact boundary. (`rule:design:evaluation-schedule`) fixes constant sharing and request memoization. No successful request bypasses independent checking. No point approximation, shortened precision sequence or weakened comparison is admitted. The finite controls contribute to the scoped close (`amend:design:bite-six-close`).

