**Rule (Accepted-act comparison premises)** · `rule:design:act-comparison-premises` The positive Reference case starts with isolated b and i, with burn {{ numval('num:numbers:act-response-raise-burn') }} and {{ numval('num:numbers:act-response-raised-target-burn') }}. Adding b→i raises i. The negative case uses the same act structure and burns {{ numval('num:numbers:act-response-lower-burn') }} and {{ numval('num:numbers:act-response-target-burn') }}; adding b→i lowers i. Both retain saturated emission and the passing full rung. Their evaluated contraction upper bounds are identical, {{ numrel('num:numbers:act-response-directions-contraction-upper') }}, despite opposite certified signs: contraction alone supplies no direction. The emission case starts with reciprocal References u→b and b→u and adds a Registration by b, retaining burns {{ numval('num:numbers:act-response-upstream-burn') }} at u and {{ numval('num:numbers:act-response-emission-burn') }} at b. Its emission changes from saturated to depleted; the emitted outward probability is strictly below the raw probability on the old equilibrium box, so emission has a nonzero transport effect. Both full rungs pass, and b decreases; its contraction {{ numrel('num:numbers:act-response-emission-contraction-upper') }}. The switch case adds b→i with burns {{ numval('num:numbers:act-response-switch-burn') }} and {{ numval('num:numbers:act-response-target-burn') }}. Previously the full rung passes with singleton supports; the new contributing width makes it fail and the anchor passes. Emission stays saturated and i increases.

**Rule (Complete act forcing)** · `rule:design:complete-act-forcing` Every comparison independently rebuilds and replays activation requests on the old equilibrium enclosure and transports that box using the new base, ledger, emission and accepted rung. The resulting full signed shock encloses g = F⁺(x⁻) − x⁻. With q₊ equal to half the new evaluated un-margined fence, the test bounds every coordinate displacement by ‖g‖∞/(1−q₊), and every loss by [q₊‖g‖∞/(1−q₊)−gᵢ]₊. No fixed-emission numerator substitution or uncertified intermediate rung is used. The signs come from the certified solve enclosures, not from contraction or the bounds alone.

