**Amendment (Bite 6 finite close)** · `amend:design:bite-six-close` Close (`gate:design:bite-6`) for the admitted fragment and finite witness scope. Independent bite-wide review accepted the fixture predicates, finite claim text, compiler prerequisite, backend soundness/domain/platform/refinement dossier, published corpus and budget disposition. The seven formerly undeclared burn/act floors now have measured assertions or minimum-supported executions and failed controls in (`rec:design:standing-floor-calibration`); purpose refusal uses identical public evidence and cross-replay, and exhausted comparisons explicitly refuse charged prices. The combined standing mint is (`rec:design:standing-witness-join`). The required-tier join must execute each required case exactly once on the close source, under one declared configuration and the registered epoch-ledger-1, epoch-compiler-1, epoch-numeric-1, graph-numeric-1 and records-numerics-1 editions with their pn-epoch-rust, pn-graph-rust and pn-records-rust implementations. The retained gate log joins HARNESS-MATRIX, CLAIM-EVIDENCE and a successful gate exit; the loop gate repeats that same-source join with the full import-base commit and external-exact tagged paper values under (`rule:design:published-act-correspondence`). A source change requires that join again. The obligation registry uses scoped-supported for this finite close, not a universal completion status. Later holds remain owned: (`open:design:backend-platform-support`) by backend maintainers and the platform reviewer; (`open:design:binding-ridge-controller-admission`) by the epoch/controller implementers in bite 7; unrestricted families and consumer guarantees by the verification implementer in bite 11 under (`open:design:core-standing-properties`); real-chain integration by the epoch, adapter and API implementers with the devnet operator under (`open:design:devnet-evidence`); deployment authentication and publication by their identity and host implementers und