**Record (Closure admission witnesses)** · `rec:design:closure-admission-witnesses` ``[EPOCH-claim:admission:closure-consumes-whole-dependent-blocks]`` checks interleaved blocks and overlapping current parents. ``[EPOCH-claim:admission:closure-registers-consecutive-recognized-markers]`` checks historical shared parents, skipped and repeated registration, pending markers and a changed predecessor. ``[EPOCH-claim:admission:closure-requires-attested-cause-and-duration]`` checks exact target/minimum and maximum boundaries with a separate attestation refusal. ``[EPOCH-claim:admission:closure-replay-binds-one-common-context]`` checks that valid foreign numerical evidence cannot be mixed with this candidate, including an equal-price schedule from different causes. The existing partition evidence remains ``[GRAPH-claim:membership:dependency-closures-partition-the-final-act-set]``, ``[GRAPH-claim:membership:small-dags-preserve-partition-and-indices]``, ``[GRAPH-claim:membership:partition-publication-requires-exact-cover]``, ``[GRAPH-claim:membership:invalid-records-never-reach-partition]``, ``[GRAPH-claim:membership:generated-partitions-match-set-oracle]`` and ``[GRAPH-claim:membership:shared-partitions-retain-complete-results]``. These are finite local admission witnesses for (`verif:design:closure-partition-cases`), not evidence of host halt or recovery, deployed policy realization or unrestricted offline histories.

**Record (Individual safety and actual support)** · `rec:design:admission-individual-controls` Under (`rule:design:admission-comparison-precision`), a separate minimum-scope unresolved probe uses target burn {{ numval('num:numbers:admission-individual-target-burn') }} and supporter burn {{ numval('num:numbers:admission-straddle-source-burn') }}. Its independently replayed positive-rung individual interval strictly straddles the wall, and admission returns IndividualSafety as INDECISIVE. This deliberately unresolved comparison sets no accuracy floor. The separate anchor support control uses target burn {{ numval('num:numbers:admission-poor-burn') }} and the same supporter. The hand-derived transported ratio clears the wall despite a lower own post-debit rate; substituting the insolvent target burn {{ numval('num:numbers:admission-insolvent-burn') }} refuses OwnSolvency. Exact anchor identities use minimum-supported scope, not a sensitivity floor. The finite claims are ``[EPOCH-claim:admission:individual-straddles-withhold-publication]`` and ``[EPOCH-claim:admission:real-support-cannot-fund-own-debits]``; both new cases retain the ordinary budget.

**Amendment (Finite admission contract join)** · `amend:design:admission-contract-join` The registered epoch-admission-1 edition with pn-epoch-rust covers the implemented rational-floor candidate gate and local closure surface under (`alg:design:atomic-final-admission`) and (`alg:design:closure-registration`). The admission, admission-review, closure and admission-contract suites share complete candidate, schedule and procedure constructors; the direct admission and closure consumers retain the same final-gate evidence and reject a foreign common context. The existing scoped claims and ``[EPOCH-claim:admission:shared-contract-retains-identical-final-gates]`` supply the evidence. The shared consumer comparison is an exact identity at the solver minimum under (`rule:design:admission-comparison-precision`), not a sensitivity floor. These are core protocol/API mechanism cases, with unchanged assertions and budgets; their required invocation follows the allowance placement rule in (`rule:harness:tiers`). This contract excludes the published complete-history join in (`open:design:reference-registration-base`), checked-ridge charged carriers, persistent atomic publication and deployment authentication. The required-tier matrix must execute the registered cases at this edition and implementation; declaration alone is not a pass.

**Open Question (Reference Registration base join)** · `open:design:reference-registration-base` Owner: the paper fixture maintainers and epoch implementer. The published reference under network-v0.31.1, ``ver:epoch:final-stamps`` and ``ver:epoch:final-backpressure``, includes Dave's Registration in the proposed act counts, but its evaluated base consists only of declared self-retention {{ numval('num:numbers:published-retention') }} and the outward vouches. Under ``def:epoch:domain-weighted-base-allocation`` and ``rem:epoch:compiled-acts-fold-into-cells``, a Registration also contributes its unit empty-coordinate coefficient to its home diagonal. With the reference's uniform unit domain weights and normalized profile, that contribution cannot vanish. The existing compiler's base_tables witness adds the Registration contribution separately from retention. The paper fixture maintainers have confirmed that the final-gate fixture must follow the complete-history base, including the Registration contribution; the tagged definition supplies no exclusion for this fixture. They will publish a repair with a complete act census and regenerated standings, gate values and certificate. This hold closes when that published repair supplies the complete-history inputs and outputs and the epoch implementation reproduces their final-stamp and headroom join without changing those inputs. Until then, no unchanged-input compiled production comparison with the superseded final stamps or headroom is claimed. The existing bite-six certified corpus remains a reproduction of its declared abstract matrix, distinct from the held complete-history join. Neither zero retention nor omission of the Registration is an admissible repair under the current declarations.

