**Amendment (Bite seven close assessment)** · `amend:design:bite-seven-close-assessment` The implemented finite scope has been reviewed against its fixture premises and claim wording: declaration refusals keep candidates distinct from publication; ridge laws remain stated analytic premises with complete-cover evidence, not sampled uniqueness; controller claims retain branch order and distinguish exact ideals from delivered rational walls; schedule claims retain lead, policy boundaries, old vintages and separate covariance and migration comparisons; admission claims retain own solvency, individual safety, the act-weighted epoch gate and immutable refusal; closure claims retain whole partitions, consecutive recognized markers, one common context and attested earliest determination rather than inferring it from timestamps. Ridge charge admission is explicit consumer selection under (`rule:design:ridge-charge-contract`). The required-tier union executes every case exactly once on one source and configuration. The retained gate log joins the registered epoch-admission-1, epoch-ledger-1, epoch-compiler-1, epoch-numeric-1, graph-numeric-1, records-numerics-1 and graph-partition-1 editions with their named implementations, HARNESS-MATRIX, CLAIM-EVIDENCE and successful gate exit. Every finite controller, ridge, schedule, admission and closure claim is joined directly in the obligation row; ordinary citations alone supply no member evidence. Public calibration is recorded in (`rec:design:graph-public-calibration-top-up`), with unresolved multi-root allowance identities still explicitly pending. This is an implementer close assessment, not a new independent mathematical review. The repository supports finite scoped closes, as (`amend:design:bite-six-close`) shows, but the declared bite-seven evidence explicitly requires the reference final-set join. Rather than remove that required comparison from the bite, (`gate:design:bite-7`) remains held solely on (`open:design:reference-registration-base`): the paper maintainers publish a repaired complete act census and regenerated standings, gates and certificate, then the epoch implementer reproduces them. The existing declared-matrix corpus remains distinct and proves no complete-history reference result. Persistent atomic application, admitted-verifier selection at persistence, authentication and host recovery remain bite eight; policy realization remains bite nine; unrestricted offline families remain bite eleven. No implemented schedule, charged floor, final gate, closure or calibration item is presented as missing.

