**Amendment (Test marker policy)** · `amend:design:test-marker-policy` Only the host operator places recognized epoch markers in the test deployment, under one policy published before genesis with immutable identity, edition, interpretation and declared cadence. This restricts recognized markers, not the paper's open burn-accumulator construction. The selected accepted-set representation is the complete list: finite lists expose all members, predecessor inclusion and current-lineage bounds directly, without another availability dependency. Conformance still exercises commitments with uniquely verifiable complete public openings, missing and ambiguous openings and both acceptance bounds under ``cond:comparator:marker-network-acceptance``. List selection does not waive lineage dependence, destruction verification, alias consistency or single counting. Placement, cadence, depth and finality assumptions must be published before enabling the deployment; their pending values are not defaults. Loss of a final marker freezes the last closed state and publishes fault evidence; the selected response is an explicit reviewed re-anchor under a newly published policy edition, naming a fresh initial marker and the ledger-continuity decision while retaining the old closed history. Neither blocks nor depth alone establish finality. A copied marker name cannot replace causal dependence under ``cond:comparator:marker-causal-dependence``. Both alternative-response conformance and the selected deployment response remain (`verif:design:finality-breach-cases`).

